# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# This file is nearly empty ON PURPOSE. The React site serves the ORIGINAL
# WordPress URLs (/aboutus/, /contactus/, /mediafeatures/ and the five
# top-level team-member pages), so the migration needs no redirects at all.
# Google sees no URL change.
#
# Do not "tidy up" the URLs without an SEO decision and a 301 plan.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# /blog 404s on the live site but is linked from the homepage cards and may be
# indexed. Send it home until the Blog is actually built.
# 302 (temporary) on purpose — a 301 would be a lie we'd have to undo.
/blog                 /                 302
/blog/*               /                 302

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPA fallback. MUST BE LAST.
# Without this, deep links like /aboutus/ reload into a 404 because the host
# looks for an /aboutus/index.html that doesn't exist.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*                    /index.html       200
